<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <StaticWebAssetBasePath>/</StaticWebAssetBasePath>
	<AddRazorSupportForMvc>true</AddRazorSupportForMvc>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>EditorAssistant.AI.Umbraco</PackageId>
	<Product>Umbraco.EditorAssistant.AI</Product>
    <Version>1.2.1</Version>
    <Authors>Alaeddin Alhamoud</Authors>
	<Copyright>Copyright © 2026 Alaeddin Alhamoud</Copyright>
    <Description>AI writing and page summaries for Umbraco 17 and 18. Generate and improve rich text with an editor toolbar assistant, and let website visitors summarize pages using a shared, securely configured AI provider.</Description>
	<PackageReleaseNotes>1.2.1 (11 November 2026)
- Support Umbraco CMS 17.7+ in the 17.x line and 18.x with one .NET 10 package; limit Umbraco dependencies to versions below 19.
- Fix startup on Umbraco 18.0 by declaring the Serilog 4.4.0 dependency explicitly, and remove the unused Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi package reference.
- Use Google.GenAI 2.1.0 for Gemini only, replacing hand-written HTTP requests. Preserve configured credentials and models, summary caching, editor cache bypass, and cancellation; combine all text parts from the first response candidate.
- Update OllamaSharp to 5.5.2, Microsoft.Extensions.AI and Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI to 10.11.0, and the client OpenAPI generator to 0.99.0.
- Add a repeatable compatibility suite and GitHub Actions workflow. Verify the same packed NuGet package on Umbraco 17.7.0, 18.0.0, and 18.3.1, and check client APIs against backoffice 18.0.0 and 18.3.1.
- Add five Gemini SDK transport tests covering request configuration and multipart text, cache bypass, empty responses, provider errors, and cancellation. All 14 server tests pass; live AI calls and browser dialogs were not exercised.
- Update compatibility and Gemini documentation and synchronize NuGet, Umbraco manifest, and backoffice display versions to 1.2.1.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageTags>umbraco;ai;assistant;openai;azure-openai;gemini;claude;deepseek;ollama;summarization</PackageTags>
	<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
	<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Alaeddinalhamoud/Umbraco.EditorAssistant.AI</PackageProjectUrl>
	<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Alaeddinalhamoud/Umbraco.EditorAssistant.AI</RepositoryUrl>
    <Product>EditorAssistant.AI.Umbraco</Product>
    <Title>EditorAssistant.AI.Umbraco</Title>
    <PackageIcon>package-icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
	<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>


  <!-- Central package management - no versions -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Google.GenAI" />
    <PackageReference Include="Umbraco.Cms.Api.Common" />
    <PackageReference Include="Umbraco.Cms.Api.Management" />
    <PackageReference Include="Umbraco.Cms.Core" />
    <PackageReference Include="Umbraco.Cms.Web.Common" />
    <PackageReference Include="Umbraco.Cms.Web.Website" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.AI" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI" />
    <PackageReference Include="OllamaSharp" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog" />
  </ItemGroup>


  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Don't include the client folder as part of packaging nuget build -->
    <Content Remove="Client\**" />

    <!-- However make the Umbraco-package.json included for dotnet pack or nuget package and visible to the solution -->
    <None Include="Client\public\umbraco-package.json" Pack="false" />
    <None Include="package-icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <Content Update="wwwroot\App_Plugins\**" Pack="true" PackagePath="wwwroot\App_Plugins\" />
  </ItemGroup>


  <ItemGroup>
    <Folder Include="wwwroot\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
